sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/55264/pg55264.txt#line=19480,19486>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/55264>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "Superposed upon the usual sinuous outline, with its “lobes” and “saddles,” we have here a minutely ramified, or arborescent outline, in which all the branches terminate in wavy, more or less circular arcs,—looking just like the ‘landscape marble’ from the Bristol Rhaetic. We have no difficulty in recognising in this a surface-tension phenomenon.".
